"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T07:35:48Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T07:35:48Z","body":"This can be worked around at export time by changing some property on the scene or on the exported collection, i.e a timestamp, to force godot to reimport `.gltf`. But of course this means having custom blender export code.\n```python\n# i.e ExportHelper child class...\n\nbpy.data.collections.get(self.collection)[\"timestamp\"] = time.time()\n\nbpy.ops.export_scene.gltf(\n    filepath=self.filepath,\n    collection=self.collection,\n    export_format='GLTF_SEPARATE',\n    export_extras=True,\n    # etc...\n)\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3803581070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]